---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site.js";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${siteConfig.name} handles data for calculators, converters, and image tools.`}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Privacy Policy" }]} />
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900 sm:text-3xl">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="prose-tool mt-6">
      <h2>Calculators and unit converters</h2>
      <p>
        Every calculator and unit converter on {siteConfig.name} (percentage, age, date, discount, length, mass,
        temperature, area, and all electrical calculators) runs entirely in your browser. The values you type are
        never transmitted to our server or anywhere else.
      </p>

      <h2>Image tools</h2>
      <p>
        Image tools default to local, in-browser processing: your file is decoded and converted on your device and
        is never uploaded. Each image tool also offers an explicitly labelled "Upload to our server for processing"
        option. If you choose that option:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your file is uploaded to our API over HTTPS (in production) and held only in memory — in an isolated worker process — for the duration of that one request.</li>
        <li>Nothing is written to disk during normal operation. The in-memory buffer and its worker are discarded as soon as the request finishes, fails, times out, or is cancelled (including if you close the tab mid-upload); none of it persists afterward.</li>
        <li>As a defensive safety net only (not the normal mechanism), the server also runs a startup and periodic sweep of its temporary-file directory, in case a future bug or crash ever left a stray file there.</li>
        <li>We do not log the contents of uploaded files or the filenames you upload.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Choosing local processing means the file itself never leaves your device — but it does not, by itself,
        prevent our hosting provider or any advertising service (if and when enabled) from collecting other data
        about your visit, such as standard web server access logs or ad-related data. Those are separate from the
        file-processing behavior described above.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        Tracking and analytics are disabled by default on this site. If that changes in the future, this policy
        will be updated to describe exactly what is collected and why, before any such tracking goes live.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Advertising (Google AdSense) is currently disabled across the entire site. If advertising is enabled in the
        future, this section will be updated to describe what it means for your data, and a consent mechanism
        appropriate to your location will be put in place first. A custom consent banner, on its own, does not
        automatically satisfy any particular advertising network's requirements — that needs to be verified
        separately when advertising is actually enabled.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting costs</h2>
      <p>
        No paid conversion APIs are used by this site. Running it still involves ordinary hosting, bandwidth, and
        domain costs, which are unrelated to how your data is processed.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      {
        siteConfig.operatorEmail ? (
          <p>
            Questions about this policy can be sent to{" "}
            <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.operatorEmail}`} class="font-semibold text-teal-700 underline">
              {siteConfig.operatorEmail}
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>A contact email has not been configured yet for this site.</p>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
